# ============================================================
# Qubit One — environment variable template (Phase 24, spec §7)
#
# Every variable is classified by scope and read-time:
#   public        → safe to expose to the browser bundle (NEXT_PUBLIC_*)
#   server-only   → MUST never reach the client bundle, logs or reports
#   system        → provided by the runtime platform; do not set manually
#
# Rules of record:
#   - NEVER commit a filled copy of this file. Real values live only
#     in the platform secret store: local `.env` (git-ignored), the
#     Vercel per-environment variable settings (production / preview
#     / development reviewed separately), or encrypted CI secrets.
#   - New environment variables must be added here (names only)
#     before their first commit (see .github/pull_request_template.md).
#   - The deployment gate (scripts/deploy/deployment-gate.ts) fails
#     when code references an undocumented variable.
# ============================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — server-only · runtime · REQUIRED
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Prisma PostgreSQL connection URL. Production = Supabase PostgreSQL
# (credentials RFC 3986 percent-encoded, ?sslmode=require appended).
# Used by: prisma/schema.prisma, src/lib/db.ts, the platform DB probe
# and /api/health. Server-only: never expose it to the browser.
DATABASE_URL=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication — server-only · runtime · required in production
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# HMAC session-signing secret (>= 32 chars). Required in production
# and preview so every serverless instance signs sessions identically.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# QUBIT_AUTH_SECRET=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment telemetry — server-only · runtime · optional
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# These enable the live provider integrations already built in the
# Operations/Observability modules (Deployment Status, Deployment
# History, Rollback Center, Deployment Impact, CI status). Without
# them those screens show "Not configured" — nothing is simulated.
# They grant read/execute access to provider APIs: server-only,
# repository-scoped where possible, never printed to logs or reports.
# VERCEL_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime metadata — system · injected by Vercel at runtime
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Listed for audit completeness. Do not set these manually.
# VERCEL_DEPLOYMENT_ID=
# VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA=
# VERCEL_ENV=
# VERCEL_REGION=
# PORT=
# NODE_ENV=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Application — server-only · reserved
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Public base URL of the deployment when reverse-proxied (Caddy
# gateway or equivalent). Reserved; currently unused by the code.
# APP_URL=
